<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kwame Nkrumah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kwame Nkrumah was the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>'s independence movement and the first prime minister and president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, which became independent in 1957. He chose the name Ghana in tribute to the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>, though the old empire lay far to the north-west. The choice reflects the empire's lasting symbolic importance in African history.</p></div>
